{{/*
family: line-cli
what: syslog
transports: udp, tcp, tls
reference: common line-oriented logging commands (logging host, logging trap, logging facility, logging source-interface); RFC 5424 severities
verification: reference
*/}}
{{define "does"}}Sends the device's log messages, {{.Severity.Word}} and more severe, to Woodshed over {{if eq .Transport "udp"}}UDP{{else if eq .Transport "tcp"}}TCP{{else}}TLS{{end}}.{{end}}

{{define "parts"}}
@@part cli - Enter in global configuration mode, then save the configuration
logging host {{.Address}} transport {{.Transport}} port {{.Port}}
logging trap {{.Severity.Line}}
{{- if .Facility}}
logging facility {{.Facility}}{{end}}
{{- if .SourceInterface}}
logging source-interface {{.SourceInterface}}{{end}}
{{end}}

{{define "notes"}}
The host command differs most between devices: some take `logging host {{.Address}}` for UDP 514 alone, some write the transport as `{{if eq .Transport "udp"}}udp{{else}}tcp{{end}}/{{.Port}}` after the address or name the sending interface before it, and some use a `logging server` command instead.
`logging trap` sets the lowest severity sent to log hosts on many devices; others set it on the host line, or accept the number ({{.Severity.Num}}) instead of the keyword.
{{- if eq .Transport "tls"}}
Import Woodshed's CA certificate as a trusted CA first (Settings → TLS → CA certificate: PEM to paste, DER to upload){{if .CASHA256}}, and compare the fingerprint the device shows with {{.CASHA256}}{{end}}. How you import it, and whether the host line names it, differs by device.
If the device checks the server's name, give it {{.TLSName}}{{if .TLSNameKnown}}, a name on Woodshed's certificate{{else}}: a DNS name on Woodshed's certificate (Settings → TLS){{end}}; many devices check names only, not IP addresses.
{{- end}}
{{- if .SourceInterface}}
The source interface's address is what Woodshed shows as the device, so pick one with a stable address.
{{- end}}
Turn on timestamps in the messages if the device offers it (with milliseconds and the time zone, where it can); Woodshed also keeps the time each message arrived.
{{end}}

{{define "check"}}The device appears on Woodshed's Dashboard with its first message; if it doesn't, check the device's log host status and Woodshed's Listeners on the Setup page.{{end}}
